(6313071, 934119, 86322, '<td valign="top">Very Well Done my friend, Congrats on the Blue, very well deserved....</td>', 'Very Well Done my friend, Congrats on the Blue, very well deserved....', '2011-02-14 12:31:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6313112, 933793, 100831, '<td valign="top">Is luxury dead?</td>', 'Is luxury dead?', '2011-02-14 12:51:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(6313121, 933793, 54645, '<td valign="top">First time seeing this. Fantastic satire.</td>', 'First time seeing this. Fantastic satire.', '2011-02-14 12:55:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6313128, 932903, 54645, '<td valign="top">You did well to maintain the shapes of your objects, not an easy task to achieve with blur. You have learned, or have always known, how to control and place your light with this style of image; same can be said about the tones. An object oriented image in which the black object doesn''t belong. Ha! That must be the kernels. If you are at three packs of smokes, they won''t be going anywhere soon! ;) &lt;stop smoking, hard to quit my day job&gt;</td>', 'You did well to maintain the shapes of your objects, not an easy task to achieve with blur. You have learned, or have always known, how to control and place your light with this style of image; same can be said about the tones. An object oriented image in which the black object doesn''t belong. Ha! That must be the kernels. If you are at three packs of smokes, they won''t be going anywhere soon! ;) <stop smoking, hard to quit my day job>', '2011-02-14 13:01:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6313130, 933847, 116574, '<td valign="top">This is so cute.  What you didn''t say in your blurb was how many shots did it take to get the right one.  Having worked with little kids and animals, sometimes is just luck in getting any shot much less one this good.  Annabelle is precious. I think my fav part is the bit of her red tongue sticking out.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-02-14 13:04:34.</i></td>', 'This is so cute.  What you didn''t say in your blurb was how many shots did it take to get the right one.  Having worked with little kids and animals, sometimes is just luck in getting any shot much less one this good.  Annabelle is precious. I think my fav part is the bit of her red tongue sticking out.', '2011-02-14 13:03:29.000000', '2011-02-14 13:04:34.000000', 0),
(6313137, 932903, 54645, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> Seriously?  I''m supposed to pick an item out of "these" that doesn''t belong?   Nope.   I don''t even know what the objects ARE!       3 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, I would say that Lydia is a very nice putz! She is a wonderful person who usually doesn''t like blur so I don''t hold it against her, at least not often! I will say that this style of imagery is best appreciated by those who also create similar images. There is a difficulty, and delicacy, to these images that is often under appreciated. Although it comes natural to the lucky few, it is mostly an acquired taste.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-02-14 15:49:50.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by LydiaToo: Seriously?  I''m supposed to pick an item out of "these" that doesn''t belong?   Nope.   I don''t even know what the objects ARE!       3   Well, I would say that Lydia is a very nice putz! She is a wonderful person who usually doesn''t like blur so I don''t hold it against her, at least not often! I will say that this style of imagery is best appreciated by those who also create similar images. There is a difficulty, and delicacy, to these images that is often under appreciated. Although it comes natural to the lucky few, it is mostly an acquired taste.', '2011-02-14 13:06:41.000000', '2011-02-14 15:49:50.000000', 0),
(6313150, 934119, 43774, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon! Excellent shot.</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon! Excellent shot.', '2011-02-14 13:10:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6313153, 933847, 43774, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the ribbon, this is so cute.</td>', 'Congratulations on the ribbon, this is so cute.', '2011-02-14 13:11:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6313156, 933138, 43774, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon!</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon!', '2011-02-14 13:11:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6313191, 932903, 30364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bspurgeon:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ubique:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> Seriously?  I''m supposed to pick an item out of "these" that doesn''t belong?   Nope.   I don''t even know what the objects ARE!       3 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No, you putz. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, I wouldn''t go that far, maybe a very nice putz! She is a wonderful person who usually doesn''t like blur so I don''t hold it against her, at least not often! I will say that this style of imagery is best appreciated by those who also create similar images. There is a difficulty, and delicacy, to these images that is often under appreciated. Although it comes natural to the lucky few, it is mostly an acquired taste. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I thought it was a term of endearment.  A sort of gentle gibe, not too harsh.  It is where I come from.<br/> <br/>ETA I looked it up.  It has a meaning I never intended, so I apologise &amp; withdraw it.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-02-14 13:45:08.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by bspurgeon: Originally posted by ubique: Originally posted by LydiaToo: Seriously?  I''m supposed to pick an item out of "these" that doesn''t belong?   Nope.   I don''t even know what the objects ARE!       3   No, you putz.   Well, I wouldn''t go that far, maybe a very nice putz! She is a wonderful person who usually doesn''t like blur so I don''t hold it against her, at least not often! I will say that this style of imagery is best appreciated by those who also create similar images. There is a difficulty, and delicacy, to these images that is often under appreciated. Although it comes natural to the lucky few, it is mostly an acquired taste.   I thought it was a term of endearment.  A sort of gentle gibe, not too harsh.  It is where I come from. ETA I looked it up.  It has a meaning I never intended, so I apologise & withdraw it.', '2011-02-14 13:37:56.000000', '2011-02-14 13:45:08.000000', 0),
