(6315833, 933138, 91372, '<td valign="top">One word describes this image for me: Balanced. <br/> <br/>Simple yet elegant in the details. Love it. Could easily be a great stock image. <br/> <br/>The one complaint that I have, and if I had voted I think it would have brought me down a point, is that the far left fork is a little bit higher than the one to the right. Kind of hurts the composition IMO. <br/> <br/>In any case, you deserve the yellow. Excellent photo.</td>', 'One word describes this image for me: Balanced.  Simple yet elegant in the details. Love it. Could easily be a great stock image.  The one complaint that I have, and if I had voted I think it would have brought me down a point, is that the far left fork is a little bit higher than the one to the right. Kind of hurts the composition IMO.  In any case, you deserve the yellow. Excellent photo.', '2011-02-15 21:56:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6316439, 933847, 5607, '<td valign="top">Fabulous image!  Congrats on you well-deserved ribbon!  These shots are never easy and you clearly had the patience to wait it out until you got the shot.  that is the mark of a good photographer....</td>', 'Fabulous image!  Congrats on you well-deserved ribbon!  These shots are never easy and you clearly had the patience to wait it out until you got the shot.  that is the mark of a good photographer....', '2011-02-16 06:48:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6316597, 934121, 103142, '<td valign="top">Sorry about the DQ. Definitely would have ribboned -- spectacular image! FYI: I''ve come across this before. It seems if you leave just a faint hint of it showing, that works, but if it disappears completely, it''s removing an aspect of the photo. Normally if you leave just a little showing, it really isn''t as distracting as you think, and then it can pass the test.</td>', 'Sorry about the DQ. Definitely would have ribboned -- spectacular image! FYI: I''ve come across this before. It seems if you leave just a faint hint of it showing, that works, but if it disappears completely, it''s removing an aspect of the photo. Normally if you leave just a little showing, it really isn''t as distracting as you think, and then it can pass the test.', '2011-02-16 09:18:29.000000', NULL, 0),
