(6322183, 934121, 30214, '<td valign="top">amazing work Christoph! Shame about DQ! Hard to tell without seeing the original of course, but I can''t imagine you (with your imagination!) could not think of some way to provide light from the right from outside the frame. I usually try to stay far away from a potential DQ territory, even at the expense of the final result, but you seem to like the thrill :).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-02-20 14:16:51.</i></td>', 'amazing work Christoph! Shame about DQ! Hard to tell without seeing the original of course, but I can''t imagine you (with your imagination!) could not think of some way to provide light from the right from outside the frame. I usually try to stay far away from a potential DQ territory, even at the expense of the final result, but you seem to like the thrill :).', '2011-02-20 13:29:07.000000', '2011-02-20 14:16:51.000000', 0),
(6322323, 934121, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> amazing work Christoph! Shame about DQ! Hard to tell without seeing the original of course, but I can''t imagine you (with your imagination!) could not think of some way to provide light from the right from outside the frame. I usually try to stay far away from a potential DQ territory, even at the expense of the final result, but you seem to like the thrill :). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Lev!<br/>I must confess I don''t particularly like being disqualified. But it is so frustrating to not shoot your best idea just because of some physical constraints ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: amazing work Christoph! Shame about DQ! Hard to tell without seeing the original of course, but I can''t imagine you (with your imagination!) could not think of some way to provide light from the right from outside the frame. I usually try to stay far away from a potential DQ territory, even at the expense of the final result, but you seem to like the thrill :).   Thanks Lev!I must confess I don''t particularly like being disqualified. But it is so frustrating to not shoot your best idea just because of some physical constraints ;-)', '2011-02-20 14:28:18.000000', NULL, 0),
